{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzB55aB7FcLHk7YVLGVr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's not dead code, but the tests don't need it right now.\n\n**What it does:** `kiln/timeparse.py:3-13` reads it. With `KILN_LEGACY_TZ=1`, `parse()` treats timestamps that have no timezone as UTC, which is how kiln worked before 2.0. Without it, they're read as local time.\n\n**Why the tests don't depend on it:**\n- Only `tests/test_timeparse.py` uses `parse()`. One test passes an explicit `+02:00` offset, so the flag doesn't apply. The other only checks that `.hour == 8`, which is true either way.\n- I ran the suite without the flag and with `TZ=America/New_York`, and all 3 tests passed.\n- `fixtures/firings.csv` has timestamps with no timezone (e.g. `2026-09-02T08:00:00`), but no script or other module calls `timeparse.parse()` on them, so seeding and `doctor.py` don't use the flag either.\n\n**So in practice** it's a leftover in step 4. It only pins tests to pre-2.0 behaviour, and current tests don't exercise that. One caveat: I can't tell from the repo whether someone wanted tests to run with UTC behaviour on purpose. If so, it would be better to set it inside the test itself rather than in SETUP.md, so nobody running plain `python3 -m unittest` gets different results.\n\nDo you want me to remove it from step 4? I could do that in the same commit as the step 2 `--db-url` fix if you want that too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":268,"cache_read_input_tokens":20660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":268},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-47>","timestamp":"2026-11-13T02:55: